Metadata filters (VectorFilter v1)

Every vector backend exposes filters differently — pgvector takes raw SQL, Pinecone takes its own JSON, Qdrant has a `must`/`should`/`must_not` tree. AgentsKit normalizes them into one `VectorFilter` shape so callers stay portable.

```ts

const filter: VectorFilter = {
  tags: { $in: ['docs', 'rag'] },
  version: { $gte: 2 },
  archived: { $ne: true },
}

const results = await store.search(embedding, { topK: 5, filter })
```

Metadata filters (VectorFilter v1) — Shape

```ts
type VectorFilter =
  | { $and?: VectorFilter[]; $or?: VectorFilter[] }
  | { [field: string]: VectorFilterPredicate }

type VectorFilterPredicate =
  | string | number | boolean | null         // shorthand for { $eq: ... }
  | { $eq: ... } | { $ne: ... }
  | { $in: [...] } | { $nin: [...] }
  | { $gt | $gte | $lt | $lte: number | string }
  | { $exists: boolean }
```

