```ts

const tools = [
  ...firecrawl({ apiKey: process.env.FIRECRAWL_API_KEY! }),
  ...reader({ apiKey: process.env.JINA_TOKEN }),
  ...documentParsers({
    parsePdf: async bytes => {
      const { default: pdf } = await import('pdf-parse')
      const r = await pdf(Buffer.from(bytes))
      return { text: r.text, pages: r.numpages }
    },
  }),
]
```

- `firecrawl_scrape` / `firecrawl_crawl` — managed scraper with JS rendering.
- `reader_fetch` — zero-dep Jina Reader wrapper; returns LLM-ready text.
- `parse_pdf` / `parse_docx` / `parse_xlsx` — BYO parser functions so you pick the native-dep story.

Multi-agent topologies — Hierarchical

A routing tree. Start at the root, descend as long as a child matches
(by tag or custom route), then execute the leaf.

```ts

const tree = hierarchical({
  root: {
    agent: triageAgent,
    children: [
      { agent: billingAgent, tags: ['refund', 'invoice', 'billing'] },
      { agent: technicalAgent, tags: ['bug', 'error', 'crash'] },
    ],
  },
  maxDepth: 3,
})
```

Unified multi-modal — In an adapter

A vision-aware adapter reads `msg.parts` and maps each entry to its
provider's shape. A text-only adapter keeps reading `msg.content` and
sees a safe projection like `"caption\n[image: pic.png]"`.

```ts

function toOpenAIMessage(m: Message) {
  const { parts } = normalizeContent(m.content, m.parts)
  return {
    role: m.role,
    content: parts.map(p => {
      if (p.type === 'text') return { type: 'text', text: p.text }
      if (p.type === 'image') return { type: 'image_url', image_url: { url: p.source, detail: p.detail } }
      return { type: 'text', text: `[${p.type}]` }
    }),
  }
}

// Quickly grab every attached image:
const images = filterParts(parts, 'image')
```

